-- Snowflake silver landing schema (EDGARTOOLS_PROD.EDGARTOOLS_SILVER_LANDING) bootstrap.
--
-- Generated by infra/scripts/generate_silver_landing_ddl.py -- regenerate with:
--   uv run python infra/scripts/generate_silver_landing_ddl.py \
--       > infra/snowflake/sql/bootstrap/11_silver_landing_schema.sql
--
-- This file is committed as a readable snapshot; the generator (reflecting
-- edgar_warehouse.silver_store._DDL via in-memory DuckDB introspection -- see
-- the generator's own module docstring for why that mechanism, not
-- SQLAlchemy reflection, is used here) is the source of truth. Regenerate
-- and diff before re-applying if silver_store.py's schema has changed.
--
-- Root cause this file exists to prevent, named per the migration map's
-- standing requirement (not generic caution): the MDM Snowflake mirror
-- schema was silently lost on a prior account cutover because it was
-- provisioned by a one-off, uncommitted manual shell session with no script
-- to re-run (CLAUDE.md, "MDM Snowflake mirror schema lost on cutover"). This
-- file is the silver-landing-zone equivalent of
-- infra/snowflake/sql/bootstrap/09_mdm_mirror_schema.sql, written before
-- this migration's first real provisioning step is ever run by hand, so the
-- same failure shape cannot repeat here.
--
-- Full design context: .scratch/silver-snowflake-migration/map.md,
-- Tickets 01 (model structure), 02 (parse_sequence/concurrency), and 05
-- (this ticket -- ownership/grants).
--
-- Run once per environment (idempotent, safe to re-run):
--   snow sql --connection edgartools-prod -f infra/snowflake/sql/bootstrap/11_silver_landing_schema.sql
--
-- Every statement is CREATE ... IF NOT EXISTS or an additive GRANT (no
-- REVOKE, no DROP, no OWNERSHIP transfer -- see CLAUDE.md's
-- "Manifest-pipeline ownership + cursor-syntax incident" for why
-- GRANT OWNERSHIP ... REVOKE CURRENT GRANTS silently strips unrelated
-- grants). Ownership: the schema, sequence, and every table are created
-- under ACCOUNTADMIN and then granted to EDGARTOOLS_PROD_LOADER -- the
-- platform's single existing dedicated pipeline-object owner, already
-- holding gold's 20 dynamic tables, the MDM mirror's 19 tables, and the
-- graph schema. Reused deliberately rather than minting a new role, per
-- this ticket's decision: a second pipeline-object owner would repeat the
-- exact ownership fragmentation the loader-role policy was created to
-- eliminate.
--
-- Deliberately narrower grant than the MDM mirror's SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/
-- DELETE: only SELECT + INSERT. Landing is append-only by design (silver-
-- snowflake-migration map, Ticket 01) -- granting UPDATE/DELETE would be a
-- standing capability with no legitimate caller, not an oversight.
--
-- Excluded from this schema: pipeline_run_lease. It is dual-listed in
-- edgar_warehouse.silver_protection.PROTECTED_TABLE_REGISTRY, but only
-- because it needed to survive the OLD whole-file candidate/canonical merge
-- -- a mechanism Ticket 02 retired outright. It's cross-execution lease
-- state (sec_fetch_active), not domain data, and it isn't append-only (a
-- lease's whole point is a mutable current status) -- it stays exactly
-- where it is today (silver_store.py's local DuckDB), unaffected by this
-- migration.
--
-- Included beyond the registry: sec_guidance_fact_reject. It's real domain
-- data (a quarantine log) that Ticket 01's Answer said explicitly stays
-- append/log-shaped in silver too, but it was never in
-- PROTECTED_TABLE_REGISTRY to begin with -- that registry was scoped to the
-- OLD cross-writer merge eligibility, and this table was deliberately
-- excluded from THAT (it has no natural key to merge on). Scoping this
-- generator strictly by registry membership silently missed it; caught
-- while building the downstream dbt silver-model generator and fixed here.

USE ROLE ACCOUNTADMIN;
USE DATABASE EDGARTOOLS_PROD;
CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS EDGARTOOLS_SILVER_LANDING;
USE SCHEMA EDGARTOOLS_SILVER_LANDING;

-- Single shared sequence: row-level parse_sequence assignment, safe under any
-- concurrency (Snowflake's metadata layer coordinates allocation globally --
-- silver-snowflake-migration map, Ticket 02's decision). One sequence across
-- every landing table, not one per table -- the window-function collapse that
-- reads this later partitions by business key per table already, so a single
-- monotonically increasing value remains a valid ordering marker regardless of
-- which table a row belongs to.
CREATE SEQUENCE IF NOT EXISTS PARSE_SEQ START = 1 INCREMENT = 1;

